## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where Feishu log messages containing emoji or other supplementary-plane Unicode characters (e.g. 🎉, 😀, 🚨) could produce garbled text with lone surrogates when a truncation boundary falls in the middle of a UTF-16 surrogate pair. This affects:

- `sanitizeLogValue` in `card-action.ts` — truncates log values at 500 code units for chat-type resolution error logs
- `formatFeishuWsErrorForLog` in `monitor.transport.ts` — truncates WebSocket error messages for log output

These two helpers were missed in the earlier sweep (c16bb8725a) that already covered `bot.ts` and `monitor.comment.ts` in the same extension.

## Why This Change Was Made

Replace raw `.slice(0, N)` with the existing `truncateUtf16Safe` helper (imported from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/text-utility-runtime`), which rounds down to the nearest safe code-point boundary instead of cutting mid-character. This is the same fix pattern that was already applied to `bot.ts:1007`, `bot.ts:1074`, and `monitor.comment.ts` in the feishu extension by the prior sweep.

## User Impact

No direct user-visible impact — these are log-level helpers. Operators reading feishu debug logs will see correctly truncated strings instead of potentially garbled characters when emoji appear near truncation boundaries.

## Evidence

**Premise — `.slice()` cuts surrogate pairs:**

```
$ node -e "
function hasLoneSurrogate(s) {
  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {
    const code = s.charCodeAt(i);
    if (code >= 0xD800 && code <= 0xDBFF) {
      if (i + 1 >= s.length || s.charCodeAt(i + 1) < 0xDC00 || s.charCodeAt(i + 1) > 0xDFFF) return true;
      i++;
    } else if (code >= 0xDC00 && code <= 0xDFFF) return true;
  }
  return false;
}
console.log('MSG:🎉 rest'.slice(0, 5), '→ lone surrogate:', hasLoneSurrogate('MSG:🎉 rest'.slice(0, 5)));
console.log('MSG:😀 rest'.slice(0, 5), '→ lone surrogate:', hasLoneSurrogate('MSG:😀 rest'.slice(0, 5)));
"
MSG:\ud83c → lone surrogate: true
MSG:\ud83d → lone surrogate: true
```

**After — `truncateUtf16Safe` rounds down to the nearest complete code point:**

The helper is already tested in `extensions/feishu/src/bot.helpers.test.ts` (added by c16bb8725a). The same function is used here via the identical import path.

**Changed files:**

- `extensions/feishu/src/card-action.ts` — `sanitizeLogValue`: `.slice(0, 500)` → `truncateUtf16Safe(x, 500)`
- `extensions/feishu/src/monitor.transport.ts` — `formatFeishuWsErrorForLog`: `.slice(0, N)` → `truncateUtf16Safe(x, N)`

**Test run:** `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/feishu/` — passed (exit 0).

**What was not tested:** Live Feishu WebSocket error logs with emoji content — log-level helpers; live credentials were not available in my checkout. The code change is mechanical and identical to the already-shipped fix in `bot.ts`.
